Z||000011||JayUSA77||06-27-2001||02:47 AM||||I know it sounds like alot but when im on the road i want to dominate it.  Im tired of people that pay 40,000 dollars for a car thinking there the #%@^. I wanna show them what some hard work and a nice engine can do.  So do you think the haftshafts need to be changed too?||||reg||1
Z||000012||BBBAD GT||06-27-2001||10:42 PM||||What kind of 1/4 mi times and mph are you turning?  If you want a transmission to last with N2O, then I would put a 2 stage unit on there with 150/100 stage so the transmission won't be hit with a 250 shot all at once.  Or you can try the variable hit units like the one from NOS or Jacobs.  <P>I sure hope you have some experience with N20 before starting out with a 250 shot.  The details (plugs/timing/fuel pump) need to be looked at much closer than like a 100-150 shot.<P>BTW, my Tremec TKO in my Stang is holding up fine to a calcuated 550 hp.  Here is a guy with a twin turbo race 331 Ford who put down almost 1,000 hp to the wheels with the same trans I have (say a prayer for that clutch).<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
